==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈneɪtəl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-natal.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪtəl|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵenh₁-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|nātālis||natal}}, from {{m|la|nātus}}, perfect active participle of {{m|la|nāscor||I am born}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵenh₁-}}. {{doublet|en|Noel}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|?}}

# Of or relating to [[birth]].
#: {{ux|en|Sea turtles return to their '''natal''' beaches to nest.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987| title=A Thousand Plateaus|author=Gilles Deleuze; Félix Guattari| page=456| passage=The constituents of the nation are a land and a people: the "'''natal'''", which is not necessarily innate, and the "popular," which is not necessarily pregiven.}}

